 What is a Branch in Git?
- A branch is simply a pointer to a commit in Git’s history.
- It represents an independent line of development.

Now to create a new branch we use <git branch name>
Now to switch to the new branch we use <git checkout branch name >
Now to list the branches in local we use <git branch>
Now to list the branches in remote we use <git branch -r>
Now to list the all branches local & remote we use <git branch -a>
Now to push the branch we use <git push origin (branch-name)>
Now to clone the remote repository we use <git clone URL>
When we clone a Git repository, the remote automatically set as origin in our local repo


Now add the repository to local we use <git remote add origin URL>
Now to add a new repository for the local we use <git remote set-url origin (url)https://github.com/Chandu950/merge.git>
