git stash

git stash is a Git command that lets you temporarily save your uncommitted changes (both staged and unstaged) without committing them, so you can switch branches, pull updates, or work on something else, and later reapply those changes.

when we done multiple git stash for different files when we want those file back we will apply <git stash apply> it will retrive the latest stashed file only and it will not delete the stash entry
if we want a specific stashed file need apply <git stash apply stash@{3}>
if we want delete the stash entry after retriving use git stash drop stash@{3}>
if we want to retrive and delete at the same time we use <git stash pop>

